{
  "paraId": "1C8E5640",
  "style": "",
  "text": "Few studies have focused on neutropenic patients with cancer and sepsis or septic shock. Neutropenic sepsis has been reported chiefly in patients with hematological malignancies, who contributed 83% of our population [20–22]. Major advances in cancer treatment and supportive care over the past two decades have contributed to broaden the criteria for ICU admission of patients with cancer [23, 24]. The older age and heavier comorbidity burden of admitted patients seen in our study during the recent period vs. the early period corroborates previous findings [25–27]."
}

